One CI step for hardware-and-silicon, plus a test that the catalogue file and the code agree.

    - name: Lanes conformance and catalogue
      run: |
        git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/YobieBenjamin/safety-governor /tmp/sg
        python3 -m pip install cryptography
        cd /tmp/sg && python3 -m lanes.check && python3 catalogue/export.py "$GITHUB_WORKSPACE" --check

tests/test_catalogue_data.py (new):

    import json, os, pathlib
    from hardware_ref.attacks import CATALOGUE

    def test_catalogue_matches_shared_data():
        path = pathlib.Path(os.environ.get("SG_CATALOGUE", "../safety-governor/catalogue/attacks.json"))
        entries = json.loads(path.read_text())["entries"]
        assert [(a.name, a.layer, a.expect, a.description) for a in CATALOGUE] == \
               [(e["name"], e["layer"], e["expect"], e["description"]) for e in entries]

Then a format change here that is not mirrored in safety-governor/lanes/fixtures fails this build,
and one made there fails this one.
